---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import ownerGuitar from "../assets/blog/one-owner-1966-gibson-es-345/original-owner-with-es345.jpeg";
import ownerAmp from "../assets/blog/one-owner-1966-gibson-es-345/original-owner-with-ampeg.jpeg";
import guitarCase from "../assets/blog/one-owner-1966-gibson-es-345/es345-in-case.jpeg";
import guitar1 from "../assets/blog/one-owner-1966-gibson-es-345/1966-gibson-es-345-1.jpg";
import guitar2 from "../assets/blog/one-owner-1966-gibson-es-345/1966-gibson-es-345-2.jpg";
import guitar3 from "../assets/blog/one-owner-1966-gibson-es-345/1966-gibson-es-345-3.jpg";
import guitar4 from "../assets/blog/one-owner-1966-gibson-es-345/1966-gibson-es-345-4.jpg";
import guitar5 from "../assets/blog/one-owner-1966-gibson-es-345/1966-gibson-es-345-5.jpg";
import guitar6 from "../assets/blog/one-owner-1966-gibson-es-345/1966-gibson-es-345-6.jpg";

const details = [
  [guitar6, "Gold Maestro vibrato on the 1966 Gibson ES-345"],
  [guitar5, "Cherry Gibson ES-345 headstock and lightly worn gold hardware"],
  [guitar4, "Bound headstock and crown inlay"],
  [guitar3, "Beautifully preserved cherry back"],
] as const;
---

<article class="es345" id="top">
  <header class="es345-hero">
    <div class="es345-hero__copy">
      <p class="es345-eyebrow">Original Owner · Connecticut · 1966</p>
      <h1>One Owner’s<br />1966 Gibson<br />ES-345</h1>
      <p class="es345-dek">He played it in Connecticut rock bands during the late 1960s, then stored it carefully after he stopped playing.</p>
      <p class="es345-byline">A 1966 Gibson ES-345 · Joe's Vintage Guitars</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="es345-hero__figure">
      <Image src={ownerGuitar} alt="The original owner holding his 1966 Gibson ES-345" width={1000} priority />
      <figcaption>The Original Owner With His ES-345 · Connecticut</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </header>

  <section class="es345-intro">
    <p>I traveled to Connecticut to buy this 1966 Gibson ES-345 from the man who purchased it new. He played it in several rock bands during the late 1960s, then stopped playing and kept the guitar safely stored. Nearly sixty years later, its cherry finish and gold hardware were still beautifully preserved. It was one of the cleanest 1960s Gibson guitars I had seen.</p>
  </section>

  <figure class="es345-full-photo">
    <Image src={guitarCase} alt="Cherry 1966 Gibson ES-345 displayed in its case in Connecticut" width={1180} />
    <figcaption>1966 Gibson ES-345 · Cherry · One Owner Provenance</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <section class="es345-chapter">
    <p class="es345-number">01</p>
    <div>
      <h2>Rock Bands in Connecticut</h2>
      <p>I met the original owner at his home in a beautiful Connecticut neighborhood. He bought the ES-345 new in 1966 and used it in several local rock bands during the late 1960s.</p>
      <p>When his years of playing in bands ended, he kept the guitar. It did not pass through dealers, collectors or a string of later owners. It remained with the same musician who selected it in 1966.</p>
      <p>That direct history came from the owner himself. I was able to see the guitar in his home, hear how he used it and photograph him holding it again.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="es345-pair">
    <figure><Image src={guitar1} alt="Front of the cherry 1966 Gibson ES-345 with gold hardware" width={760} /><figcaption>Cherry Finish · Gold Hardware</figcaption></figure>
    <figure><Image src={guitar2} alt="The 1966 Gibson ES-345 with its same year Ampeg amplifier" width={760} /><figcaption>The ES-345 With Its Same Year Ampeg</figcaption></figure>
  </section>

  <blockquote>The Cherry Finish, Gold Hardware, and Original-Owner History Stayed Together for Nearly Sixty Years.</blockquote>

  <section class="es345-chapter">
    <p class="es345-number">02</p>
    <div>
      <h2>A Carefully Preserved One Owner Gibson</h2>
      <p>A clear ownership history matters with a vintage guitar. This ES-345 came directly from the original owner, along with his account of buying it new and playing it during the late 1960s.</p>
      <p>The cherry finish retains strong gloss with little visible edge wear. The gold hardware, split parallelogram inlays, Varitone control, and Maestro vibrato remain together. After seeing it in person, I would grade the guitar near mint.</p>
      <p>Seeing the guitar in person made the preservation even more striking. It looked as though the owner had put it away much earlier in its life and taken care of it ever since.</p>
      <p>My <a href="/post/gibson-es-345-history-value/">Gibson ES-345 history and value guide</a> covers the model's stereo wiring, Varitone circuit, year-by-year features, and authentication points.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="es345-detail-grid" aria-label="Details of the 1966 Gibson ES-345">
    {details.map(([src, caption]) => <figure><Image src={src} alt={caption} width={760} /><figcaption>{caption}</figcaption></figure>)}
  </section>

  <section class="es345-amp">
    <div>
      <p class="es345-eyebrow">The Original Musical Pairing</p>
      <h2>The 1966 Ampeg Amplifier</h2>
      <p>The owner also sold me his Ampeg amplifier from 1966. He had owned the amp alongside the ES-345, so the two pieces arrived together with the same history.</p>
      <p>The photograph shows him standing with the Ampeg at his Connecticut home. Buying the guitar and its same year amplifier directly from their original owner made this a memorable trip.</p>
      <p>The model badge is not readable in the photograph, so I am leaving the amplifier model unassigned until it can be confirmed.</p>
    </div>
    <Image src={ownerAmp} alt="The original owner standing beside his 1966 Ampeg amplifier" width={900} />
  </section>

  <section class="es345-explore">
    <p class="es345-eyebrow">Explore Joe's Vintage Guitars</p>
    <h2>More for Vintage Guitar Owners</h2>
    <div>
      <a href="/free-appraisal/"><b>01</b><strong>Get a Free Guitar Appraisal</strong><small>Learn what your vintage guitar may be worth.</small></a>
      <a href="/how-to-read-gibson-serial-numbers/"><b>02</b><strong>Read Gibson Serial Numbers</strong><small>Find helpful information for identifying and dating a Gibson.</small></a>
      <a href="/sell-my-gibson-guitar/"><b>03</b><strong>Sell Your Vintage Gibson</strong><small>Talk directly with Joe about your instrument.</small></a>
      <a href="/blog/"><b>04</b><strong>Discover More Guitar Stories</strong><small>Meet the instruments and owners behind the history.</small></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="es345-closing">
    <Image src={guitarCase} alt="The cherry 1966 Gibson ES-345 in its case" width={900} />
    <div>
      <p class="es345-eyebrow">The Next Chapter</p>
      <h2>Preserving the Complete Story</h2>
      <p>This ES-345 and Ampeg spent close to sixty years with the man who bought them in 1966. The guitar's condition, the matching year amplifier and the owner's photographs preserve a history that could easily have been lost.</p>
      <p>I am grateful that he trusted me with both pieces and took the time to share their story.</p>
      <a href="/blog/">Read More Guitar Stories</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</article>

<style>
  .es345 { --e-ink:#231f1a; --e-paper:#f5f0e8; --e-rust:#a03a1e; --e-dark:#682412; --e-gold:#c29a61; background:var(--e-paper); color:var(--e-ink); overflow:hidden; }
  .es345 * { box-sizing:border-box; }
  .es345 figure { margin:0; }
  .es345 :global(img) { display:block; width:100%; height:100%; object-fit:cover; }
  .es345-eyebrow,.es345-number,.es345-byline,.es345 figcaption { font:600 11px/1.5 var(--font-display,Oswald),sans-serif; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.15em; }
  .es345-eyebrow,.es345-number { color:var(--e-gold); }
  .es345-hero { min-height:790px; padding-top:185px; display:grid; grid-template-columns:46% 54%; background:#181410; color:#fff; }
  .es345-hero__copy { padding:90px clamp(30px,6vw,95px); align-self:center; }
  .es345 h1 { margin:25px 0 30px; color:#fff; font:600 clamp(58px,7vw,108px)/.91 var(--font-display,Oswald),sans-serif; letter-spacing:-.035em; }
  .es345-dek { max-width:560px; margin:0; color:#e2d7c6; font-size:clamp(20px,2vw,27px); line-height:1.5; }
  .es345-byline { margin-top:42px; color:#9f9283; }
  .es345-hero__figure { min-height:605px; position:relative; }
  .es345-hero__figure :global(img) { object-position:center 35%; }
  .es345 figcaption { color:#fff; background:rgba(20,16,12,.7); padding:9px 12px; position:absolute; right:22px; bottom:20px; }
  .es345-intro { max-width:1080px; margin:auto; padding:82px 150px; }
  .es345-intro p { margin:0; color:#3c332a; font-size:23px; line-height:1.75; }
  .es345-full-photo { position:relative; max-width:1120px; height:min(65vw,720px); margin:0 auto 76px!important; }
  .es345-chapter { max-width:1040px; margin:auto; padding:78px 40px; border-top:1px solid #d6ccbd; display:grid; grid-template-columns:95px 1fr; gap:45px; }
  .es345-chapter h2,.es345-amp h2,.es345-explore h2,.es345-closing h2 { margin:0 0 32px; font:600 clamp(42px,5vw,70px)/1.05 var(--font-display,Oswald),sans-serif; }
  .es345-chapter p:not(.es345-number),.es345-amp p:not(.es345-eyebrow),.es345-closing p:not(.es345-eyebrow) { margin:0 0 24px; font-size:18px; line-height:1.8; }
  .es345-pair,.es345-detail-grid { max-width:1120px; margin:10px auto 76px; display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:22px; }
  .es345-pair figure,.es345-detail-grid figure { height:520px; position:relative; }
  .es345-detail-grid figure { height:410px; }
  .es345 blockquote { max-width:1120px; margin:0 auto 76px; padding:55px 80px; background:var(--e-dark); color:#eedfc0; font:600 clamp(30px,4vw,52px)/1.15 var(--font-display,Oswald),sans-serif; text-transform:uppercase; }
  .es345-amp { padding:80px max(45px,calc((100vw - 1100px)/2)); background:#e8dcc8; display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:64px; align-items:center; }
  .es345-amp>div { max-width:550px; }
  .es345-amp :global(img) { height:580px; }
  .es345-amp h2 { margin-top:14px; }
  .es345-amp .es345-eyebrow,.es345-explore .es345-eyebrow,.es345-closing .es345-eyebrow { color:var(--e-rust); }
  .es345-explore { max-width:1100px; margin:auto; padding:85px 30px; }
  .es345-explore h2 { margin:12px 0 38px; }
  .es345-explore>div { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; border-top:1px solid #cfc1ad; }
  .es345-explore a { padding:26px 18px; display:grid; grid-template-columns:38px 1fr; border-bottom:1px solid #cfc1ad; color:inherit; text-decoration:none; }
  .es345-explore a:nth-child(odd) { border-right:1px solid #cfc1ad; }
  .es345-explore b { color:var(--e-rust); font-family:var(--font-display,Oswald),sans-serif; }
  .es345-explore strong { font:600 19px var(--font-display,Oswald),sans-serif; }
  .es345-explore small { grid-column:2; margin-top:5px; color:#6d6256; font-size:13px; }
  .es345-closing { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1.05fr .95fr; background:#181410; color:#fff; }
  .es345-closing :global(img) { height:630px; }
  .es345-closing>div { padding:95px 70px; }
  .es345-closing h2 { color:#fff; margin-top:14px; }
  .es345-closing p:not(.es345-eyebrow) { color:#ded4c5; }
  .es345-closing a { display:inline-block; margin-top:18px; padding:15px 22px; background:#eedfc0; color:#3e2a14; font:600 12px var(--font-display,Oswald),sans-serif; text-decoration:none; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.08em; }
  @media (max-width:900px) {
    .es345-hero { grid-template-columns:1fr; padding-top:150px; }
    .es345-hero__copy { padding:65px 26px; }
    .es345-hero__figure { min-height:95vw; }
    .es345-intro { padding:58px 25px; }
    .es345-intro p { font-size:20px; }
    .es345-full-photo { width:calc(100% - 40px); height:75vw; }
    .es345-chapter { grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:10px; padding:56px 25px; }
    .es345-pair,.es345-detail-grid { grid-template-columns:1fr; margin-right:20px; margin-left:20px; }
    .es345-pair figure,.es345-detail-grid figure { height:auto; min-height:70vw; }
    .es345 blockquote { margin-right:20px; margin-left:20px; padding:38px 28px; }
    .es345-amp,.es345-closing { grid-template-columns:1fr; padding:0; }
    .es345-amp>div,.es345-closing>div { padding:60px 25px; }
    .es345-amp :global(img),.es345-closing :global(img) { height:100vw; }
    .es345-explore>div { grid-template-columns:1fr; }
    .es345-explore a:nth-child(odd) { border-right:0; }
  }
</style>
